cfbase-mactypes.patch
Licence: this patch changes a file of Apple's CF-476.19 and is under that release's licence (Apple
Public Source License 2.0, APPLE_LICENSE in the release).

What: CFBase.h takes the Carbon base types (UInt32, SInt32, OSStatus, Boolean, FourCharCode, OSType,
...) from <MacTypes.h> instead of <libkern/OSTypes.h>.
Why: CF-476.19 is the open-source CF-Lite, which is built without Carbon headers and so declares
its base types from the kernel's OSTypes.h (and, where that is missing, in CFBase.h itself). The
CoreFoundation of iPhone OS is built with MacTypes.h (CarbonHeaders-18.1, installed as published),
and the other frameworks rely on that: AudioToolbox and CoreAudio use FourCharCode, OSType and the
MacTypes definitions of the integer types through CoreFoundation. With MacTypes.h included,
CFBase.h's own fallback declarations are skipped (they are guarded by !defined(__MACTYPES__)).
libkern/OSTypes.h is not installed in this sysroot.
Affects: every unit that includes a CoreFoundation header (all Objective-C units, audiod, airplay,
cspot's Apple sinks); without the change they do not compile.

--- a/System/Library/Frameworks/CoreFoundation.framework/Headers/CFBase.h
+++ b/System/Library/Frameworks/CoreFoundation.framework/Headers/CFBase.h
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@
 #include <AvailabilityMacros.h>
 
     #if defined(__MACH__)
-        #include <libkern/OSTypes.h>
+        #include <MacTypes.h>
     #endif
 
 #if !defined(__MACTYPES__)
